{"v":1,"built_at":"2026-10-29T17:14:57.698Z","core":{"appSha":"22f65844ea8d","builtAt":"2026-10-29T16:34:22.543Z","schemaV":1},"key":"us/119-hr-4307","model":{"found":true,"billKey":"us/119-hr-4307","polity":"us","eyebrow":"United States","reference":"H.R. 4307","title":"Enhancing Detection of Human Trafficking Act","titleExpandable":false,"meta":"Education and Workforce Committee · Rep. Tim Walberg (R-MI)","summary":{"lead":"Official summary (Congressional Research Service, Public Law): ","blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Enhancing Detection of Human Trafficking Act","gap":"none"},{"kind":"para","text":"This act requires the Department of Labor to provide training and education to its employees on how to effectively assist law enforcement in detecting human trafficking.","gap":"para"},{"kind":"para","text":"The act directs Labor to determine which employees should receive the training and education based on their official duties. Further, it requires the training and education to include information that is appropriate for the employees' location or environment; that reflects current trends and best practices for the location or environment; and that is relevant to detecting human trafficking, identifying suspected victims, and referring potential cases to the Department of Justice and other appropriate authorities.","gap":"para"}]},"pathLabel":"The legislative path","latest":{"labelText":"Signed by Pres. Trump","glyph":{"icon":"scroll","badge":true},"date":"20 October 2026"},"asOf":{"lead":"Record as of ","date":"20 October 2026","note":"the most recent action in the official record. Status can lag; each step below carries its own date."},"groups":[{"spine":{"key":"rec-H.R. 4307-17","kind":"record","spine":true,"date":"20 October 2026","labelText":"Signed by Pres. Trump","glyph":{"icon":"scroll","badge":true},"postId":"us-20261021-c5edb832","postHref":"/p/us-20261021-c5edb832","whatsNext":{"lead":"What's next: ","text":"Takes effect (on enactment unless the text se